   "id": 505985,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate <span data-math=\"2.5 \\times {10^5} - 9.8 \\times {10^6}\">2.5 \\times {10^5} - 9.8 \\times {10^6}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"2.5 \\times {10^5} - 9.8 \\times {10^6}\"></span></p>\n<p>First, you need to make the powers of 10 match.</p>\n<p>Make them both have an exponent of 6. Move the decimal point one place to the left on the first number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.25 \\times {10^6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Because the powers of 10 match, use the distributive property to factor the power of 10 from the numbers. Then, subtract the other part of the numbers separately.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.25 \\times {10^6} - 9.8 \\times {10^6}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(0.25 - 9.8) \\times {10^6}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 9.55 \\times {10^6}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\" - 9.55 \\times {10^6}\">- 9.55 \\times {10^6}</span>"
    }
   ],
